22. In Ciba Ltd. Basle Switzerland v. M.Ramalingam and S.Subramaniam Trading in the name of Sought Indian Manufacturing Co., Madura and Another AIR 1958 Bombay 56 (V 25 C 21 ) on the use of word Cibol; the explanation furnished by the defendant that C stands for cuts, I for itches,
B for boils and "OL for oil, the court rejected this explanation as patently untrue and dishonest;
it was held that at the time when the application for registration had been made by the respondent they were not thinking of curing humanity of cuts, itches and boils, but only of ring worms.
